{
  "_readme": [
    "Human-curated list of instance maps. tools/mapdata.py turns this into Data/Instances.lua.",
    "Art lives at Interface\\WorldMap\\<folder>\\<stem><floor>_<tile> (floors) or <stem><tile> (a single 'page').",
    "alts: tried in order; the addon uses the first whose art exists in the running client.",
    "flavors: which clients list it in the map menu (vanilla, tbc, forever). Any client can still open it from a shared pack.",
    "maps: the IDs in the game's Map table the instance is played on (GetInstanceInfo's instanceID), so a new board made inside it starts on its map.",
    "folder: optional when every floor comes from minimap or images.",
    "floorNames: overrides for floors retail data cannot name (keys are floor numbers, '0' = page).",
    "minimap: floors shown from a map's own minimap tiles, for instances with no drawn map (keys are floor numbers; each replaces that floor of the folder's art). cols and rows pick the tiles world/minimaps/<map>/map<col>_<row>; origin and content are the window onto that block to show, in pixels.",
    "images: floors shown from an image the addon ships as Art\\<file>.tga (keys as for minimap). tools/stitch.py makes them and prints their size and content.",
    "verified: clients where someone has eyeballed the art and confirmed it is the right layout.",
    "note: shown in the report only."
  ],
